1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,400
A buyer might pay 1,500 USDC.
The store offers Ayşe 600 today.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
So she borrows 600 instead.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,070
Kaya Rug House certifies the rug.

4
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:14,130
Kaya signs in a real wallet.

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,717
Ayşe now owns the certificate.

6
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,200
Ayşe borrows 600 USDC for 6 months.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,850
Fees come off once, up front.
She gets 540.00 USDC.

8
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:28,320
Deniz lends 600 and gets 645.00 back.

9
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,880
One transaction funds the loan.

10
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:34,330
A buyer turns up. Ayşe repays 600.

11
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,600
The loan cost $60.
Selling cheap would lose $900.

12
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:43,117
Two signatures close the certificate.
Ayşe takes the rug home.

13
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:47,820
No repayment? The store must buy
at its own price.

14
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:50,580
The store can't lowball her.

15
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:54,570
Each line here links to its own transaction.

16
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:58,850
Every step is a Testnet transaction
you can check.
